                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "I knew this was going to be a Mario clone since I was aware of this series history, and I have played Twisted Dreams before. But I couldn't finish this as I had enough.\n\nIt wasn't the repetitive boss fight or the awkward power ups or the cheap looking graphics or broken achievements that made me stop. It was the jumping. More specifically, jump underneath a ceiling. During the game you have to make jumps over dangerous pits. For the most part this is fine as most of the levels are open and give you plenty of room even with enemies and hazards in the way. But during the few times you have to a jump in a small hallway, hitting the ceiling kills any momentum you have and you fall into the pit and die. And when they started doing that with spikes on the ceiling, I said to myself I was done.\n\nSo yeah, this isn't that great Mario clone. And if you want to play a game with the singular Giana Sister, just play Twisted Dream.",
